8. PAGE-BY-PAGE IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS
8.1 Authentication
Login
Provide:
- Email/username field.
- Password field with show/hide control.
- Accessible labels and inline validation.
- Submit loading state and disabled state during submission.
- Generic authentication failure message.
- Registration/recovery links only if those backend workflows are enabled.
- Session-expired and access-denied states.
Use the existing session/authentication mechanism. Do not store passwords, access tokens, refresh tokens or session identifiers in localStorage or sessionStorage. Do not implement password hashing or session issuance in the frontend.
Registration and recovery
The SRS says the registration mode must be chosen before implementation. Keep self-registration/invitation-based registration configurable and document the pending decision. Only build the corresponding UI when the existing backend flow supports it. Account recovery is conditional on an existing recovery API.
8.2 Dashboard
Build an overview dashboard with:
- Current workspace/project context.
- Project/time-range filters.
- Accessible project count.
- Registered target count.
- Assessment run count.
- Active jobs count.
- Finding severity/status distribution when available.
