8.13 Behavior Dependency Graph — Semester 8
Use @xyflow/react if compatible with the existing dependency set.

Graph requirements:
- Nodes represent API operations/resources.
- Directed edges represent producer/consumer relationships.
- Pan, zoom, fit-to-view and search/filter.
- Clear node/edge labels.
- Selected node/edge detail panel.
- Legend and accessible status descriptions.
Show provenance/review categories that match API data, such as Documented, Observed/Gathered, Inferred/Schema-derived, Approved and Rejected. Show confidence, rationale, evidence and reviewer information if available.

Inferred edges must look different from observed/documented edges. An edge or its approval must never be presented as authorization to execute a sequence. Execution still requires an approved run plan, target authorization, scope and relevant safety approvals.

Optimize large graphs with memoized custom nodes/edges and stable callbacks. The SRS's temporary usability target is a graph around 150 operation nodes and 300 edges; validate performance on the declared demo machine rather than promising a fixed result.
